{"nodes": [{"id": "build_css_p2_docs_javascript_pages_phase_6_iteration_and_destructuring_spread_with_iterables_two_operations_one_syntax_array_call_spread", "label": "Array and call spread", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "build-css-p2/docs/javascript/pages/phase-6-iteration-and-destructuring/spread-with-iterables/two-operations-one-syntax.html", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "In array literals and argument lists, ... consumes an iterable via Symbol.iterator. Plain objects throw TypeError."}, {"id": "build_css_p2_docs_javascript_pages_phase_6_iteration_and_destructuring_spread_with_iterables_two_operations_one_syntax_object_spread", "label": "Object spread", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "build-css-p2/docs/javascript/pages/phase-6-iteration-and-destructuring/spread-with-iterables/two-operations-one-syntax.html", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Copies own enumerable properties. Does not need an iterable. Spreading a Map/Set/Date/class instance yields {} or method-less objects."}, {"id": "build_css_p2_docs_javascript_pages_phase_6_iteration_and_destructuring_spread_with_iterables_two_operations_one_syntax_spread_vs_rest", "label": "Spread vs rest", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "build-css-p2/docs/javascript/pages/phase-6-iteration-and-destructuring/spread-with-iterables/two-operations-one-syntax.html", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Same three dots, opposite directions. Rest collects on the left or in parameters (must be last, only one). Spread expands on the right or in a call."}, {"id": "build_css_p2_docs_javascript_pages_phase_6_iteration_and_destructuring_spread_with_iterables_two_operations_one_syntax_spread_is_shallow", "label": "Spread is shallow", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "build-css-p2/docs/javascript/pages/phase-6-iteration-and-destructuring/spread-with-iterables/two-operations-one-syntax.html", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "MDN: multidimensional arrays are not safe to copy with spread. Use structuredClone for a genuinely independent graph; shallow is usually the right default."}, {"id": "build_css_p2_docs_javascript_pages_phase_6_iteration_and_destructuring_spread_with_iterables_two_operations_one_syntax_conditional_object_spread", "label": "Conditional object-spread no-op", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "build-css-p2/docs/javascript/pages/phase-6-iteration-and-destructuring/spread-with-iterables/two-operations-one-syntax.html", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Spreading a non-object into an object is silently a no-op, which makes ...(cond && { key }) work."}], "edges": [{"source": "build_css_p2_docs_javascript_pages_phase_6_iteration_and_destructuring_spread_with_iterables_two_operations_one_syntax_array_call_spread", "target": "build_css_p2_docs_javascript_pages_phase_6_iteration_and_destructuring_spread_with_iterables_two_operations_one_syntax_object_spread", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "build-css-p2/docs/javascript/pages/phase-6-iteration-and-destructuring/spread-with-iterables/two-operations-one-syntax.html", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "build_css_p2_docs_javascript_pages_phase_6_iteration_and_destructuring_spread_with_iterables_two_operations_one_syntax_array_call_spread", "target": "build_css_p2_docs_javascript_pages_phase_6_iteration_and_destructuring_spread_with_iterables_two_operations_one_syntax_spread_vs_rest", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "build-css-p2/docs/